    "mnemonic": "It's <kanji>all</kanji> <kanji>nature</kanji> out there. It's <vocabulary>entirely</vocabulary> nature and <vocabulary>not at all</vocabulary> city. \n\nThis word is weird. It means two opposite things. Thanks Japanese! Just look out for a negative word after the <ja>全然</ja>. If it is negative it's \"not at all\" if it's not negative it might be \"entirely.\"",
